cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TerraFlow in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TerraFlow: A Reproducible, Uncertainty-Aware Geospatial Workflow for Agricultural Suitability Modelling and Foundation-Model Inference"
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-06-08"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gmarupilla/AgroTerraFlow"
url: "https://terraflow.marupilla.dev"
abstract: >
  TerraFlow is an open-source Python library for reproducible, auditable
  geospatial workflows in agricultural and environmental data science.
  It provides a config-driven pipeline for raster ingestion, ROI clipping,
  spatial climate interpolation (linear, IDW, or Ordinary Kriging with
  LOOCV variogram selection), suitability scoring with Monte-Carlo
  uncertainty propagation, global sensitivity analysis (Sobol' / Morris),
  spatial block cross-validation, and provenance-tracked artifact export.
  Every run produces a deterministic content-addressed fingerprint enabling
  independent verification of results.
keywords:
  - geospatial
  - agriculture
  - reproducibility
  - raster
  - climate
  - workflow
  - Python
  - kriging
  - sensitivity-analysis
  - uncertainty-quantification
authors:
